{"annotationScore": 4.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "8774350", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "10702483", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "11282392", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "16895553", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "17576170", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "20176268", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "22158414", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Immunoglobulins, also known as antibodies, are membrane-bound or secreted glycoproteins produced by B lymphocytes. In the recognition phase of humoral immunity, the membrane-bound immunoglobulins serve as receptors which, upon binding of a specific antigen, trigger the clonal expansion and differentiation of B lymphocytes into immunoglobulins-secreting plasma cells. Secreted immunoglobulins mediate the effector phase of humoral immunity, which results in the elimination of bound antigens (PubMed:20176268, PubMed:22158414). The antigen binding site is formed by the variable domain of one heavy chain, together with that of its associated light chain. Thus, each immunoglobulin has two antigen binding sites with remarkable affinity for a particular antigen. The variable domains are assembled by a process called V-(D)-J rearrangement and can then be subjected to somatic hypermutations which, after exposure to antigen and selection, allow affinity maturation for a particular antigen (PubMed:17576170, PubMed:20176268). IgD is the major antigen receptor isotype on the surface of most peripheral B cells, where it is coexpressed with IgM. The membrane-bound IgD (mIgD) induces the phosphorylation of CD79A and CD79B by the Src family of protein tyrosine kinases. Soluble IgD (sIgD) concentration in serum is below those of IgG, IgA, and IgM but much higher than that of IgE. IgM and IgD molecules present on B cells have identical V regions and antigen-binding sites. After the antigen binds to the B cell receptor, the secreted form sIgD is shut off. IgD is a potent inducer of TNF, IL1B, and IL1RN. IgD also induces release of IL6, IL10, and LIF from peripheral blood mononuclear cells. Monocytes seem to be the main producers of cytokines in vitro in the presence of IgD (PubMed:10702483, PubMed:11282392, PubMed:16895553, PubMed:8774350)"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "11282392", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "16895553", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "20176268", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Immunoglobulins are composed of two identical heavy chains and two identical light chains; disulfide-linked (PubMed:20176268). An IgD molecule contains thus a delta heavy chain combined with either a kappa or a lambda light chains. Kappa light chains are found predominantly on the membrane IgD (mIgD) form and lambda on the secreted IgD (sIgD) form, this fact is poorly understood. Membrane-bound IgD molecules are non-covalently associated with a heterodimer of CD79A and CD79B (PubMed:11282392, PubMed:16895553)"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "11282392", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "20176268", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "22158414", "source": "PubMed"}], "id": "SL-0243", "value": "Secreted"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "11282392", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "20176268", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "id": "22158414", "source": "PubMed"}], "id": "SL-0039", "value": "Cell membrane"}}]}, {"commentType": "CAUTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "This sequence is an example of a full-length immunoglobulin delta heavy chain"}]}], "entryAudit": {"entryVersion": 34, "firstPublicDate": "2017-03-15", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-11-04", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2017-03-15", "sequenceVersion": 1}, "entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "extraAttributes": {"countByCommentType": {"CAUTION": 1, "FUNCTION": 1, "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION": 1, "SUBUNIT": 1}, "countByFeatureType": {"Chain": 1, "Compositional bias": 2, "Disulfide bond": 6, "Domain": 4, "Glycosylation": 8, "Region": 3}, "uniParcId": "UPI00005D3C72"}, "features": [{"description": "Immunoglobulin delta heavy chain", "featureId": "PRO_0000439284", "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 512}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 1}}, "type": "Chain"}, {"description": "Ig-like 1", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "id": "PRU00114", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 97}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 1}}, "type": "Domain"}, {"description": "Ig-like 2", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "id": "PRU00114", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 227}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 135}}, "type": "Domain"}, {"description": "Ig-like 3", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "id": "PRU00114", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 392}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 304}}, "type": "Domain"}, {"description": "Ig-like 4", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "id": "PRU00114", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 502}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 396}}, "type": "Domain"}, {"description": "Variable (V) domain, involved in antigen recognition", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "id": "6806818", "source": "PubMed"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 129}, "start": {"modifier": "EXA